[12.8284, "o", "\u001b[38;5;208m● belay\u001b[0m\r\n  **> All 18 July transactions categorized automatically — nothing left to sort by hand, and the annual car insurance was caught the moment it landed.**\r\n\r\n  - **Income:** €2,800 (salary, on schedule)\r\n  - **Car:** €505.04 — includes the confirmed €420 yearly insurance charge (expected, flagged since onboarding) + normal fuel\r\n  - **Groceries:** €309.14 — right at the ~€321/mo baseline\r\n  - **Dining out:** €36.32 — a bit under its usual ~€57/mo\r\n  - **Subscriptions:** €23.96 — Streamflix + Cloudtunes, steady\r\n  - **Card refills (main → credit):** €454.46, correctly excluded from income/spend"]
[12.8285, "o", "\r\n\r\n  No budget.md existed for July (the first draft was for August), so I compared against the historical baseline instead — nothing looked off. On the accidental re-downloads: they ingested cleanly, 122 duplicate rows on `main` and 305 on `credit` were recognized and skipped automatically, no double-counting.\r\n\r\n  Nothing new discovered this month — no forgotten subscriptions turned up, no unmatched transfers. Full letter and numbers are in `finance/months/2026-07/reports/letter_2026-07.md`, `report_2026-07.html`, and `reconciliation_2026-07.xlsx`.\r\n\r\n  One open question: **should I backfill a budget.md for July for the record**, or leave it as an actuals-only month since it predates your first draft? I defaulted to leaving it as-is — say the word if you'd rather have it filled in.\r\n\r\n  Next natural step is closing out August's plan whenever you're ready (`/monthly-prep`)."]
[12.8285, "o", "\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
